cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Caustic: hallucination detection and repair for language models from the orbit partition of a relation"
abstract: >-
  A model can know a fact and still be unable to reach it. When it cannot,
  distinct entities collapse onto one answer. Caustic treats that collapse
  as a topological invariant of the orbit partition of a relation: it is
  measurable with no ground truth and bounded from below by a theorem. The
  same bound then selects the intervention, including the noise level to
  add and whether to intervene at all.
